1
00:00:03,718 --> 00:00:05,690
<i>Number one
K-content channel.</i>

2
00:00:05,771 --> 00:00:07,685
<i>tvN for joy.</i>

3
00:00:09,005 --> 00:00:10,244
{\an8}<i>Fifteen.</i>

4
00:00:10,324 --> 00:00:11,464
{\an8}THE FOLLOWING PROGRAM IS
NOT SUITABLE FOR VIEWERS UNDER 15.

5
00:00:11,545 --> 00:00:12,712
{\an8}VIEWER DISCRETION IS ADVISED.

6
00:00:12,793 --> 00:00:13,894
{\an8}THIS PROGRAM CONTAINS PRODUCT PLACEMENTS
AND VIRTUAL ADVERTISING.

7
00:00:46,466 --> 00:00:49,886
{\an8}MY BIAS, MY BOSS

8
00:00:49,966 --> 00:00:50,898
PRODUCTION SUPPORTED BY:
MINISTRY OF CULTURE, SPORTS AND TOURISM

9
00:00:50,978 --> 00:00:51,891
KOREA CREATIVE CONTENT AGENCY

10
00:00:51,971 --> 00:00:52,867
THIS DRAMA
IS A WORK OF FICTION

11
00:00:52,947 --> 00:00:53,900
CHILD AND ANIMAL SCENES WERE FILMED SAFELY
UNDER EXPERT SUPERVISION

12
00:00:55,198 --> 00:00:57,408
Luni, what does it mean
if someone gives you a bottle of wine

13
00:00:57,492 --> 00:00:59,744
and says it's from her heart?

14
00:01:00,995 --> 00:01:03,664
In fact, that wine is said
to help one's love come true.

15
00:01:04,123 --> 00:01:06,209
<i>That means more than interest.</i>

16
00:01:06,542 --> 00:01:08,836
<i>It's normally used
to express a head-on romance.</i>

17
00:01:08,920 --> 00:01:12,048
A head-on romance?

18
00:01:12,131 --> 00:01:15,510
<i>That woman definitely likes you.</i>

19
00:01:20,932 --> 00:01:22,016
CHAN

20
00:01:29,482 --> 00:01:32,527
<i>Da-reum, I'll be out of town
for a few days from tomorrow.</i>

21
00:01:32,944 --> 00:01:35,947
<i>Could we meet up at least
for a moment before I leave?</i>

22
00:01:39,575 --> 00:01:40,660
So she

23
00:01:41,661 --> 00:01:42,870
likes me?

24
00:02:17,697 --> 00:02:19,824
Let's go. I'll walk you home.

25
00:02:19,907 --> 00:02:21,242
No, thank you.

26
00:02:21,325 --> 00:02:24,579
I need to stop by somewhere.
I'll go by myself.

27
00:02:24,662 --> 00:02:27,999
But still, I should walk you...

28
00:02:28,082 --> 00:02:30,418
Mr. Kang, are you okay?

29
00:02:31,210 --> 00:02:32,753
Of course, I'm fine.

30
00:02:33,254 --> 00:02:34,547
Why wouldn't I be?

31
00:02:35,256 --> 00:02:36,632
You seem a little off.

32
00:02:36,716 --> 00:02:38,009
Your face is all red.

33
00:02:42,346 --> 00:02:44,098
- Just go away.
- What?

34
00:02:44,181 --> 00:02:46,601
I take back walking you home.
It's canceled.

35
00:02:46,684 --> 00:02:47,768
Go on already.

36
00:02:48,603 --> 00:02:49,604
Bye.

37
00:02:50,146 --> 00:02:53,941
Okay, I'll be going then.

38
00:03:01,115 --> 00:03:02,199
Goodbye.

39
00:03:13,544 --> 00:03:15,671
This one is obviously way heavier.

40
00:03:15,755 --> 00:03:17,548
Same amount, my foot.

41
00:03:18,257 --> 00:03:21,135
How come my own mother
cares more about Ha-gi than me?

42
00:03:21,802 --> 00:03:22,928
It's ridiculous.

43
00:03:31,270 --> 00:03:32,313
What on earth?

44
00:03:33,147 --> 00:03:34,565
Why is a girl
coming out of this house?

45
00:03:35,608 --> 00:03:37,860
Tell me. Who is she?

46
00:03:38,235 --> 00:03:40,029
{\an8}Why would your employee come
all the way to your house?

47
00:03:40,112 --> 00:03:41,822
{\an8}And what's with those romantic eyes?

48
00:03:42,657 --> 00:03:45,409
{\an8}I had an urgent proposal to finish.
She was here to help. Happy now?

49
00:03:45,493 --> 00:03:48,162
{\an8}She looked familiar, though.

50
00:03:50,623 --> 00:03:52,041
{\an8}The nosebleed! The big ice ball!

51
00:03:52,124 --> 00:03:54,251
She's that crazy drunk girl, right?

52
00:03:55,795 --> 00:03:58,005
{\an8}So she works for you now?

53
00:03:58,089 --> 00:03:59,215
{\an8}Mind your own business.

54
00:04:02,218 --> 00:04:03,928
{\an8}Is that wine?

55
00:04:04,512 --> 00:04:06,681
{\an8}So much for work.
You two are totally a thing.

56
00:04:07,181 --> 00:04:09,975
{\an8}I didn't set it up.
She brought it over

57
00:04:10,226 --> 00:04:11,352
{\an8}saying it was from her heart.

58
00:04:11,435 --> 00:04:13,646
{\an8}Wait, so she confessed to you?

59
00:04:18,192 --> 00:04:19,193
{\an8}Well...

60
00:04:19,819 --> 00:04:21,404
She hasn't said it out loud.

61
00:04:21,487 --> 00:04:24,740
Mr. Kang, have this and cheer up.

62
00:04:25,366 --> 00:04:26,450
Good luck.

63
00:04:29,036 --> 00:04:32,456
But she sneaks up to cheer me on.

64
00:04:32,540 --> 00:04:33,708
<i>Mr. Kang!</i>

65
00:04:36,252 --> 00:04:37,503
I'll move next to you.

66
00:04:38,963 --> 00:04:40,840
She randomly puts her hands on me.

67
00:04:42,007 --> 00:04:43,217
Oh, man.

68
00:04:43,676 --> 00:04:44,677
Above all...

69
00:04:49,557 --> 00:04:50,891
She smiles at me
every time she sees me.

70
00:04:53,811 --> 00:04:56,814
She must have feelings for me, right?

71
00:04:58,691 --> 00:04:59,734
No.

72
00:05:01,986 --> 00:05:02,987
At that point...

73
00:05:04,655 --> 00:05:06,365
it's love.

74
00:05:07,658 --> 00:05:08,659
What...

75
00:05:09,910 --> 00:05:11,078
Love?

76
00:05:13,789 --> 00:05:14,874
Love.

77
00:05:18,419 --> 00:05:19,420
Love.

78
00:05:29,388 --> 00:05:32,183
COULD WE MEET UP AT LEAST
FOR A MOMENT BEFORE I LEAVE?

79
00:05:34,643 --> 00:05:37,313
LEE CHAN OFFICIAL
HAS STARTED A LIVE STREAM

80
00:05:37,396 --> 00:05:40,399
TUNE IN RIGHT NOW!

81
00:05:41,734 --> 00:05:43,944
<i>Hi. It's been a while, right?</i>

82
00:05:45,529 --> 00:05:48,407
<i>I have an early start tomorrow,
so I can't stay long.</i>

83
00:05:50,159 --> 00:05:51,202
I went live

84
00:05:51,869 --> 00:05:54,455
because I just wanted to see you,
even if it was like this.

85
00:05:56,624 --> 00:06:00,002
<i>I can't see you, but you can see me.</i>

86
00:06:04,131 --> 00:06:06,217
There's something
I wanted to tell you in person.

87
00:06:07,468 --> 00:06:08,928
<i>I might have hurt you</i>

88
00:06:09,470 --> 00:06:11,388
<i>because I wasn't careful at times</i>

89
00:06:12,014 --> 00:06:14,266
<i>but thank you
for always supporting me.</i>

90
00:06:15,434 --> 00:06:17,895
That's how I truly feel.

91
00:06:24,777 --> 00:06:26,529
<i>I read in my favorite book</i>

92
00:06:27,696 --> 00:06:30,199
<i>that sincerity eventually
shines through over time.</i>

93
00:06:31,867 --> 00:06:34,203
I hope my sincerity
reaches you as well.

94
00:06:41,043 --> 00:06:42,461
<i>Gosh, it's late.</i>

95
00:06:42,711 --> 00:06:44,505
<i>I should go to bed now.</i>

96
00:06:45,965 --> 00:06:47,258
<i>I'll be back. Bye.</i>

97
00:06:50,511 --> 00:06:51,512
THE LIVE STREAM HAS ENDED

98
00:06:59,728 --> 00:07:01,564
DA-REUM

99
00:07:01,647 --> 00:07:04,859
<i>Chan, I'm afraid
I don't have time today.</i>

100
00:07:04,942 --> 00:07:06,110
<i>Let's catch up later.</i>

101
00:07:06,694 --> 00:07:09,530
<i>And I'm okay
with what happened that day.</i>

102
00:07:09,822 --> 00:07:11,282
<i>Please don't let it bother you.</i>

103
00:07:13,742 --> 00:07:15,369
<i>Thanks for texting me back, Da-reum.</i>

104
00:07:16,495 --> 00:07:17,913
<i>Have a safe trip to your shoot.</i>

105
00:07:18,163 --> 00:07:19,290
<i>I'll be rooting for you from afar.</i>

106
00:07:21,083 --> 00:07:22,710
I'LL BE ROOTING FOR YOU FROM AFAR

107
00:07:37,308 --> 00:07:40,102
APPELLO

108
00:07:40,269 --> 00:07:41,562
Get a grip, Kang Ha-gi.

109
00:07:42,104 --> 00:07:43,230
Act normal.

110
00:07:45,024 --> 00:07:46,442
Just keep it normal.

111
00:08:08,923 --> 00:08:09,924
Thank

112
00:08:11,175 --> 00:08:12,217
you...

113
00:08:12,968 --> 00:08:15,220
Mr. Kang, did you find
any more stickers at home?

114
00:08:15,888 --> 00:08:17,848
Yesterday felt like a treasure hunt.
It was really fun.

115
00:08:18,307 --> 00:08:20,142
- If you find more...
- Ms. Nam.

116
00:08:20,476 --> 00:08:21,560
Yes?

117
00:08:21,810 --> 00:08:23,187
We're at work.

118
00:08:25,230 --> 00:08:26,231
I'm the CEO.

119
00:08:26,315 --> 00:08:27,316
CEO

120
00:08:28,067 --> 00:08:29,068
And you're an employee.

121
00:08:29,151 --> 00:08:30,152
EMPLOYEE

122
00:08:31,028 --> 00:08:32,571
Keep your personal

123
00:08:32,655 --> 00:08:33,656
and work life

124
00:08:33,906 --> 00:08:34,949
separate, okay?

125
00:08:50,047 --> 00:08:51,048
Goodness.

126
00:08:56,178 --> 00:08:58,639
<i>The doors are closing.</i>

127
00:08:58,722 --> 00:09:00,724
Wait, Mr. Kang!

128
00:09:00,808 --> 00:09:02,393
Mr. Kang, let me...

129
00:09:04,520 --> 00:09:05,854
What was that about?

130
00:09:06,981 --> 00:09:08,565
What's wrong with him
this early in the morning?

131
00:09:10,275 --> 00:09:12,069
Did I mess up again?

132
00:09:18,617 --> 00:09:20,536
Excuse me. Sorry.

133
00:09:22,079 --> 00:09:23,455
The CEO is going to call me in a bit.

134
00:09:23,539 --> 00:09:25,374
Make some room, please.

135
00:09:25,624 --> 00:09:26,750
Why would he call you?

136
00:09:27,167 --> 00:09:29,294
Why else? Look at that.

137
00:09:29,378 --> 00:09:32,089
The K-Wave project is worth
a massive 1.5 billion won.

138
00:09:33,048 --> 00:09:34,925
- Check this out.
- Oh, really?

139
00:09:35,009 --> 00:09:36,010
{\an8}K-SWEETNESS
TO SATISFY YOUR 5 SENSES!

140
00:09:36,301 --> 00:09:38,804
"A <i>Dalgona </i>keychain
that tastes sweet when you lick it."

141
00:09:38,887 --> 00:09:40,806
Is this really the best
an adult could come up with?

142
00:09:40,889 --> 00:09:41,974
It's a 100 percent fail.

143
00:09:43,600 --> 00:09:46,020
If you carry that around,
it's totally going to attract bugs.

144
00:09:47,021 --> 00:09:48,272
I hope it works out.

145
00:09:48,814 --> 00:09:50,774
- What's with that look?
- Let's start the meeting.

146
00:09:53,819 --> 00:09:55,320
K-WAVE PROJECT
INTERNAL CONTEST RESULTS

147
00:09:55,404 --> 00:09:56,530
We took internal submissions

148
00:09:56,613 --> 00:09:59,533
for the K-Wave project hosted
by the Korea Heritage Service, right?

149
00:09:59,742 --> 00:10:01,702
Today, I'll announce the winner.

150
00:10:02,369 --> 00:10:03,537
Since there's only one spot

151
00:10:03,787 --> 00:10:05,289
for the fashion category
in this project

152
00:10:05,372 --> 00:10:07,416
the choice of item was crucial.

153
00:10:07,708 --> 00:10:08,876
The chosen idea is

154
00:10:10,461 --> 00:10:11,462
Lee...

155
00:10:16,592 --> 00:10:18,427
Min-a's Mosaic <i>Bojagi</i>.

156
00:10:23,390 --> 00:10:24,433
- Congrats!
- Congratulations.

157
00:10:25,559 --> 00:10:26,894
- Sit back down.
- Sit down quickly.

158
00:10:26,977 --> 00:10:28,145
Min-a, congratulations.

159
00:10:29,646 --> 00:10:30,773
This is awesome.

160
00:10:30,856 --> 00:10:32,483
Ms. Min-a, please come up
and walk us through it.

161
00:10:33,067 --> 00:10:34,234
Yes, sir.

162
00:10:37,738 --> 00:10:38,989
Incredible!

163
00:10:46,288 --> 00:10:47,998
Hello.

164
00:10:48,248 --> 00:10:51,085
I'm Lee Min-a, a new hire
on the Merchandising...

165
00:10:54,171 --> 00:10:55,839
- Team.
- She's nervous.

166
00:10:58,383 --> 00:10:59,468
Well...

167
00:10:59,551 --> 00:11:02,846
My proposed item is the Mosaic <i>Bojagi</i>

168
00:11:02,930 --> 00:11:05,641
inspired by the traditional
patchwork wrapping cloth.

169
00:11:05,724 --> 00:11:09,478
The plan is to collaborate
with Geosang fabric shop in Jongno

170
00:11:09,561 --> 00:11:12,397
which has been around
for three generations.

171
00:11:14,274 --> 00:11:16,693
The patchwork wrapping cloth

172
00:11:16,777 --> 00:11:19,822
closely resembles mosaics
and stained glass.

173
00:11:19,905 --> 00:11:23,325
I expect it to feel familiar
to international customers too.

174
00:11:24,451 --> 00:11:25,494
It's so pretty.

175
00:11:25,577 --> 00:11:26,745
That's all. Thank you.

176
00:11:27,996 --> 00:11:28,997
Awesome!

177
00:11:31,416 --> 00:11:34,962
Marketing and Merchandising
will work on this project together.

178
00:11:35,212 --> 00:11:36,213
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

179
00:11:50,936 --> 00:11:53,480
What's that? It's so cute.

180
00:11:54,690 --> 00:11:56,650
A fan of mine drew this character.

181
00:11:56,733 --> 00:11:58,110
It's so cute
that I've got it all memorized.

182
00:11:58,694 --> 00:12:00,320
What's this supposed to be, though?

183
00:12:00,571 --> 00:12:01,905
A bear or a pig?

184
00:12:04,533 --> 00:12:07,452
Good point. It has a pig's nose

185
00:12:07,536 --> 00:12:10,289
- but a bear's ears.
- I'd say it's a pig.

186
00:12:13,208 --> 00:12:14,585
They're looking for the styling team.

187
00:12:15,085 --> 00:12:17,129
- Okay, we'll head over.
- Thanks.

188
00:12:19,214 --> 00:12:20,966
- Chan.
- Oh, thank you.

189
00:12:22,176 --> 00:12:24,970
I honestly don't know where you'd be
without that photo book.

190
00:12:25,596 --> 00:12:28,390
What makes it so special that you
carry it around like a lucky charm?

191
00:12:29,016 --> 00:12:30,684
It just...

192
00:12:33,520 --> 00:12:34,521
makes me feel better.

193
00:12:37,941 --> 00:12:40,402
Whenever I doubt myself

194
00:12:40,944 --> 00:12:43,780
wondering if I should
continue with this career

195
00:12:44,156 --> 00:12:45,490
or if people will still love me...

196
00:12:47,826 --> 00:12:50,662
this book cheers me on to keep going.

197
00:12:51,121 --> 00:12:53,373
The fan who made this
probably has no idea

198
00:12:53,874 --> 00:12:55,792
that it became
your most treasured item.

199
00:12:57,211 --> 00:12:58,795
I don't think she's still my fan.

200
00:12:59,421 --> 00:13:00,797
It's been ten years.

201
00:13:02,633 --> 00:13:04,051
True, so much time has passed.

202
00:13:04,343 --> 00:13:07,012
Who stays that devoted
for such a long time?

203
00:13:08,096 --> 00:13:11,016
<i>I adored you for 12 years.
I can tell that much.</i>

204
00:13:11,266 --> 00:13:13,852
You are a good person.

205
00:13:14,144 --> 00:13:17,356
If you tried to be
a good person so far

206
00:13:17,731 --> 00:13:20,734
that alone makes you a good person.

207
00:13:26,531 --> 00:13:27,741
Actually, there is.

208
00:13:28,325 --> 00:13:29,493
There's one.

209
00:13:31,703 --> 00:13:34,831
SE CORPORATION

210
00:13:38,710 --> 00:13:40,963
What are SE's cars doing here?

211
00:13:43,715 --> 00:13:46,551
No way. Just a moment, please.

212
00:13:47,803 --> 00:13:50,013
GEOSANG FABRIC SHOP

213
00:13:50,097 --> 00:13:51,473
Thank you
for making the right decision.

214
00:13:51,556 --> 00:13:52,599
My pleasure.

215
00:13:54,268 --> 00:13:55,269
Sir.

216
00:13:58,021 --> 00:13:59,856
Hello, Ms. Lee.

217
00:13:59,940 --> 00:14:02,484
What's going on here?

218
00:14:03,193 --> 00:14:05,737
You remember we're signing
the contract today, right?

219
00:14:05,821 --> 00:14:07,406
Well, the thing is...

220
00:14:07,864 --> 00:14:10,534
Listen, I'm sorry.

221
00:14:10,617 --> 00:14:15,289
SE brought us a similar offer first.

222
00:14:16,164 --> 00:14:18,125
And their terms were far better.

223
00:14:18,208 --> 00:14:20,002
But sir.

224
00:14:20,502 --> 00:14:22,587
I showed you

225
00:14:22,671 --> 00:14:24,673
this Mosaic Bojagi
before anyone else.

226
00:14:25,090 --> 00:14:26,883
How could SE possibly know...

227
00:14:27,801 --> 00:14:29,136
Ideas can

228
00:14:30,595 --> 00:14:32,514
overlap, can't they?

229
00:14:32,681 --> 00:14:33,682
Excuse me?

230
00:14:37,519 --> 00:14:40,439
Ms. Nam? That's none of your concern.

231
00:14:40,522 --> 00:14:41,898
The operations team
will take care of it.

232
00:14:43,400 --> 00:14:44,401
What?

233
00:14:54,119 --> 00:14:55,120
I'm sorry.

234
00:14:57,456 --> 00:14:59,916
Canceling on the day of the contract?
That makes no sense.

235
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:01,626
They even snatched our workshop.

236
00:15:01,835 --> 00:15:04,755
It seems they're trying to block us
from bidding altogether.

237
00:15:04,838 --> 00:15:07,507
We've been backstabbed by SE
way too many times.

238
00:15:07,591 --> 00:15:09,801
At this rate,
it's definitely an inside job.

239
00:15:09,885 --> 00:15:11,636
We need to root them out, sir.

240
00:15:11,720 --> 00:15:13,972
Are you suggesting
there's a spy among us?

241
00:15:14,056 --> 00:15:16,641
- What other explanation is there?
- Listen.

242
00:15:17,434 --> 00:15:18,477
I also had...

243
00:15:19,895 --> 00:15:21,146
the same thought for a while.

244
00:15:22,939 --> 00:15:24,107
But my conclusion was

245
00:15:24,858 --> 00:15:27,486
not to recklessly suspect
my own Appello people.

246
00:15:32,407 --> 00:15:35,786
Right now, winning this bid is
what matters most.

247
00:15:35,869 --> 00:15:38,455
Everyone, focus on coming up
with a backup item.

248
00:15:38,538 --> 00:15:39,539
- Yes, sir.
- Gosh.

249
00:15:39,623 --> 00:15:41,458
The deadline is in ten days.

250
00:15:41,541 --> 00:15:43,502
- My <i>Dalgona </i>keychain...
- Let's stop here.

251
00:15:44,419 --> 00:15:46,421
But the <i>Dalgona</i>...

252
00:15:46,505 --> 00:15:47,881
- We don't have much time...
- I'm sorry.

253
00:15:47,964 --> 00:15:49,257
I apologize.

254
00:16:03,563 --> 00:16:04,564
COCOTALK

255
00:16:10,779 --> 00:16:12,614
LEE CHAN'S SCHEDULE CHAT

256
