512
00:33:23,811 --> 00:33:26,063
I have no words for merchants.

513
00:33:28,649 --> 00:33:29,900
Get out now.

514
00:33:44,248 --> 00:33:45,708
What now?

515
00:33:49,003 --> 00:33:51,130
Ms. Nam, you've done enough here.

516
00:33:51,922 --> 00:33:54,258
I'll drop you off at the bus terminal
so head back to Seoul without me.

517
00:33:55,176 --> 00:33:56,469
What about you, sir?

518
00:33:58,679 --> 00:34:00,431
I'm not leaving
until I convince Master Im.

519
00:34:01,474 --> 00:34:04,143
I became certain
after seeing her in person.

520
00:34:08,689 --> 00:34:09,773
Then...

521
00:34:10,816 --> 00:34:12,193
I'll stay too.

522
00:34:13,152 --> 00:34:14,487
I'll do whatever I can to help.

523
00:34:15,571 --> 00:34:16,614
What are you going to do?

524
00:34:20,201 --> 00:34:22,203
I should do whatever I can.

525
00:34:25,164 --> 00:34:26,165
Ms. Da-reum.

526
00:34:34,009 --> 00:34:37,221
We Koreans look out for each other.

527
00:34:37,304 --> 00:34:39,432
You're making a mountain of kimchi.

528
00:34:39,515 --> 00:34:40,599
How could I just walk away?

529
00:34:40,683 --> 00:34:42,435
Let me help out just a little.

530
00:34:42,726 --> 00:34:45,271
Should I season
the pickled napa cabbage?

531
00:34:46,689 --> 00:34:49,900
Your arms are as thin
as a pair of chopsticks.

532
00:34:49,984 --> 00:34:51,277
Have you made kimchi before?

533
00:34:51,944 --> 00:34:53,446
It's not an easy feat.

534
00:34:54,947 --> 00:34:57,241
I may not look it,
but I helped my mom

535
00:34:57,324 --> 00:34:59,076
for a good few years.

536
00:35:02,913 --> 00:35:05,082
- Pitch in already.
- Okay.

537
00:35:07,585 --> 00:35:09,211
Make sure to coat the outsides.

538
00:35:09,295 --> 00:35:10,880
- Like this?
- Spread it out.

539
00:35:12,548 --> 00:35:15,342
A farmhand from Seoul
is willing to help out.

540
00:35:15,634 --> 00:35:16,677
- What?
- Gosh...

541
00:35:17,136 --> 00:35:18,387
- A farmhand?
- How cute.

542
00:35:18,471 --> 00:35:21,223
- That looks heavy. Give me that.
- Don't be too eager.

543
00:35:21,307 --> 00:35:22,391
It looks heavy.

544
00:35:26,770 --> 00:35:27,855
The napa cabbages are pickled.

545
00:35:27,938 --> 00:35:29,148
He has chopsticks for arms too.

546
00:35:29,940 --> 00:35:31,567
- He's pretty useful, though.
- They go here?

547
00:35:32,318 --> 00:35:35,154
You have chopstick arms
and so does he.

548
00:35:35,821 --> 00:35:37,072
You look too weak.

549
00:35:37,406 --> 00:35:39,116
- He'll be of use somewhere.
- Give me that.

550
00:35:39,658 --> 00:35:41,160
Can he even lift chopsticks to eat?

551
00:35:42,453 --> 00:35:43,579
{\an8}EYES ONLY FOR YOU, PARK SEO-JIN

552
00:35:47,708 --> 00:35:50,961
<i>Push, push, push it away</i>

553
00:35:51,295 --> 00:35:54,089
<i>Push away the dirt in your heart</i>

554
00:35:56,926 --> 00:35:58,093
To the beat.

555
00:35:58,886 --> 00:36:00,638
Did you tell Da-reum where to go?

556
00:36:00,721 --> 00:36:01,847
You bet.

557
00:36:02,306 --> 00:36:03,766
She was with a coworker.

558
00:36:03,849 --> 00:36:04,975
They looked really busy.

559
00:36:05,059 --> 00:36:06,268
- Right?
- Yes.

560
00:36:06,352 --> 00:36:08,812
Working at that huge company in Seoul

561
00:36:08,896 --> 00:36:10,523
must be really hard on her.

562
00:36:11,023 --> 00:36:14,777
She works at SE Corporation
of all places.

563
00:36:14,860 --> 00:36:17,238
- There must be lots to do.
- SE Corporation?

564
00:36:17,321 --> 00:36:19,698
That's weird. It wasn't called that.

565
00:36:21,450 --> 00:36:22,493
What do you mean?

566
00:36:22,868 --> 00:36:23,994
It wasn't called SE?

567
00:36:24,495 --> 00:36:26,038
- Pell-something.
- What?

568
00:36:26,330 --> 00:36:27,456
Pell...

569
00:36:27,790 --> 00:36:30,167
It sounded like pell... Oh, right.

570
00:36:32,503 --> 00:36:34,880
Appello. That's where she works.

571
00:36:36,173 --> 00:36:37,883
{\an8}APPELLO
NAM DA-REUM

572
00:36:37,967 --> 00:36:38,968
{\an8}What's this?

573
00:36:39,969 --> 00:36:41,387
"Appello"?

574
00:36:56,277 --> 00:36:57,695
- Ms. Da-reum.
- Yes?

575
00:36:58,153 --> 00:36:59,196
Do better.

576
00:36:59,572 --> 00:37:02,491
You're not supposed to smack it.
You're coating the leaves.

577
00:37:02,783 --> 00:37:05,452
Follow the grain
so it gets everywhere.

578
00:37:06,161 --> 00:37:07,246
So it seeps in.

579
00:37:09,540 --> 00:37:12,042
Like this? Is this what you do?

580
00:37:12,668 --> 00:37:14,670
You crushed all the leaves.

581
00:37:14,837 --> 00:37:16,297
Be more gentle.

582
00:37:16,380 --> 00:37:17,715
More caring, okay?

583
00:37:19,258 --> 00:37:22,886
You care about details
with everything.

584
00:37:23,262 --> 00:37:26,974
Once I set my mind to it,
I go all out.

585
00:37:36,567 --> 00:37:38,360
- I'm wearing this again.
- What?

586
00:37:40,446 --> 00:37:42,781
I thought the cast
would be the last of it.

587
00:37:45,826 --> 00:37:47,953
Wait. The red rubber gloves.

588
00:37:48,287 --> 00:37:50,414
Did you actually

589
00:37:51,332 --> 00:37:52,374
wear them?

590
00:38:00,174 --> 00:38:01,592
You burst into a fury and said

591
00:38:01,675 --> 00:38:04,553
you had to watch your back and front

592
00:38:04,637 --> 00:38:06,847
and that you couldn't
let your guard down.

593
00:38:08,474 --> 00:38:09,475
Did you wear them?

594
00:38:12,728 --> 00:38:14,855
I did wear them, okay?

595
00:38:15,314 --> 00:38:17,483
You swore you wouldn't.

596
00:38:17,733 --> 00:38:19,151
Jeez.

597
00:38:21,236 --> 00:38:22,446
Weren't they nice?

598
00:38:23,781 --> 00:38:24,865
Don't ask.

599
00:38:25,032 --> 00:38:27,618
- Do better.
- I am doing better.

600
00:38:27,701 --> 00:38:29,286
Your napa cabbage is almost...

601
00:38:29,620 --> 00:38:31,497
Mi-ja!

602
00:38:35,334 --> 00:38:36,335
Mom.

603
00:38:43,258 --> 00:38:44,760
What are you doing here?

604
00:38:50,224 --> 00:38:51,225
You!

605
00:38:52,685 --> 00:38:53,977
Give me those gloves.

606
00:38:54,978 --> 00:38:57,439
- What?
- Go over there

607
00:38:57,523 --> 00:38:59,441
and help move the kimchi.

608
00:38:59,525 --> 00:39:01,068
Give me the rubber gloves!

609
00:39:02,319 --> 00:39:03,696
Okay...

610
00:39:12,246 --> 00:39:13,330
Move.

611
00:39:18,377 --> 00:39:19,420
Mom...

612
00:39:22,548 --> 00:39:23,590
Master Im.

613
00:39:30,055 --> 00:39:31,348
Master Im.

614
00:39:32,266 --> 00:39:35,227
Please give my daughter a chance.

615
00:39:36,395 --> 00:39:38,731
She doesn't do a shoddy job,
whatever it is.

616
00:39:39,398 --> 00:39:42,443
With your help, she'll do great.

617
00:39:46,071 --> 00:39:47,406
The kimchi looks amazing.

618
00:39:48,198 --> 00:39:50,534
You bought
some quality napa cabbages.

619
00:39:51,160 --> 00:39:52,327
Look at the color.

620
00:39:55,372 --> 00:39:57,708
When you're done

621
00:39:58,125 --> 00:39:59,376
you need to wrap each head carefully.

622
00:39:59,918 --> 00:40:01,503
The more seasoning, the better.

623
00:40:09,678 --> 00:40:10,929
Look at you.

624
00:40:11,346 --> 00:40:12,639
You look good today.

625
00:40:13,891 --> 00:40:16,602
Should I not have registered
for a group lesson too?

626
00:40:16,685 --> 00:40:18,687
I can't have
all the ladies falling for me

627
00:40:19,062 --> 00:40:20,147
when Mi-mi's right there.

628
00:40:22,775 --> 00:40:25,110
Take a long step backward
with your right foot

629
00:40:25,194 --> 00:40:26,862
and go down and count one.

630
00:40:28,363 --> 00:40:29,406
Two.

631
00:40:30,240 --> 00:40:31,658
Again, one

632
00:40:32,910 --> 00:40:33,952
and two.

633
00:40:34,745 --> 00:40:36,121
Again, one.

634
00:40:36,747 --> 00:40:38,791
Arms forward, Mr. Min-woo.

635
00:40:39,041 --> 00:40:40,793
Strengthen your core.

636
00:40:40,959 --> 00:40:43,796
Keep your back straight
and strengthen your core.

637
00:40:44,713 --> 00:40:45,839
Watch your core.

638
00:40:45,923 --> 00:40:48,675
Keep your arms down
and watch your core.

639
00:40:48,759 --> 00:40:51,762
That's it. Keep this posture. Two.

640
00:40:53,055 --> 00:40:55,098
Again, one.

641
00:40:55,182 --> 00:40:57,059
Breathe in and straighten your back.

642
00:40:57,142 --> 00:40:59,186
Your arms should be up here.

643
00:40:59,978 --> 00:41:02,856
Why are you so weak?

644
00:41:03,524 --> 00:41:04,983
And two.

645
00:41:05,526 --> 00:41:07,444
- Get back up, Mr. Min-woo.
- Okay.

646
00:41:08,821 --> 00:41:11,406
This is the last count. One...

647
00:41:15,494 --> 00:41:17,955
SMOOTH PILATES

648
00:41:18,288 --> 00:41:19,957
- What, really?
- Yes.

649
00:41:22,918 --> 00:41:24,586
Don't be silly.

650
00:41:26,880 --> 00:41:28,173
Oh, my gosh.

651
00:41:28,799 --> 00:41:29,842
Min-woo.

652
00:41:30,634 --> 00:41:33,053
Come here. We're leaving.

653
00:41:33,136 --> 00:41:34,596
Where to?

654
00:41:34,680 --> 00:41:35,848
Where else?

655
00:41:35,931 --> 00:41:37,933
To your welcome dinner, of course.

656
00:41:38,016 --> 00:41:40,018
- I don't need one.
- Let's go.

657
00:41:40,102 --> 00:41:41,353
- Come along.
- But I...

658
00:41:42,062 --> 00:41:43,897
- What do you like?
- Goodbye.

659
00:41:43,981 --> 00:41:45,482
- Meat.
- You're not coming?

660
00:41:45,566 --> 00:41:47,150
- Bye.
- See you.

661
00:41:54,658 --> 00:41:56,285
- Take this, please.
- Sure.

662
00:41:56,785 --> 00:41:57,870
Oh, dear.

663
00:41:58,996 --> 00:42:00,122
It's so hot.

664
00:42:02,791 --> 00:42:05,627
- Ms. Da-reum. I'll take it.
- Thanks.

665
00:42:08,046 --> 00:42:09,506
Where did Mi-ja go?

666
00:42:09,590 --> 00:42:13,594
- Tell your mom dinner's ready.
- Okay.

667
00:42:25,188 --> 00:42:26,189
Mom.

668
00:42:44,875 --> 00:42:46,877
Thanks for your help.

669
00:42:49,004 --> 00:42:50,839
After all I went through
to raise you...

670
00:42:54,217 --> 00:42:58,221
What work do you do
that you're here making kimchi?

671
00:43:02,267 --> 00:43:04,353
Mom, actually...

672
00:43:05,812 --> 00:43:07,773
There's something I didn't tell you.

673
00:43:10,525 --> 00:43:11,526
I...

674
00:43:15,656 --> 00:43:18,450
I quit SE Corporation.

675
00:43:20,619 --> 00:43:21,620
I know.

676
00:43:24,706 --> 00:43:27,417
- You know?
- It's Appello or something.

677
00:43:27,501 --> 00:43:28,585
I saw your business card.

678
00:43:35,759 --> 00:43:37,344
I'm sorry I lied.

679
00:43:39,262 --> 00:43:42,140
You were so pleased
that I got into SE Corporation.

680
00:43:42,599 --> 00:43:44,601
I didn't want to let you down.

681
00:43:45,268 --> 00:43:49,189
I'm not upset
that you left a huge corporation.

682
00:43:53,026 --> 00:43:54,695
You didn't tell me.

683
00:43:55,862 --> 00:43:57,155
That's what hurts.

684
00:44:00,617 --> 00:44:03,578
Wouldn't it have been nice
if you'd told me

685
00:44:03,662 --> 00:44:06,123
you were having
a hard time at school?

686
00:44:06,873 --> 00:44:09,001
I know it's because
you don't want me to worry

687
00:44:11,003 --> 00:44:13,755
but I wonder
if it's because you don't trust me.

688
00:44:15,674 --> 00:44:18,385
Each time you keep something from me

689
00:44:20,971 --> 00:44:22,305
I get really upset.

690
00:44:33,108 --> 00:44:34,276
I'm sorry.

691
00:44:36,111 --> 00:44:37,404
I won't do it again.

692
00:44:42,659 --> 00:44:43,785
But Mom.

693
00:44:44,119 --> 00:44:46,246
It's a small company

694
00:44:46,663 --> 00:44:50,667
but they use my ideas,
and I can voice my opinion.

695
00:44:51,793 --> 00:44:52,878
I feel...

696
00:44:55,505 --> 00:44:58,425
like I can be of use there.

697
00:44:58,967 --> 00:45:01,219
That's why I like Appello

698
00:45:03,305 --> 00:45:05,140
and I'm happier there.

699
00:45:14,024 --> 00:45:15,358
Then all is well.

700
00:45:16,109 --> 00:45:19,029
Whether you work at a big
or a small company, all I want...

701
00:45:21,406 --> 00:45:22,866
is for you to be happy.

702
00:45:36,713 --> 00:45:38,340
Thank you, Mom.

703
00:45:49,768 --> 00:45:50,852
Don't cry.

704
00:46:03,615 --> 00:46:05,700
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

705
00:46:06,535 --> 00:46:08,203
- You too?
- How is it?

706
00:46:08,286 --> 00:46:10,205
- I'll get more meat.
- Okay.

707
00:46:12,707 --> 00:46:14,793
Ma'am, have some of this.

708
00:46:15,794 --> 00:46:16,962
And this.

709
00:46:17,879 --> 00:46:19,047
Thanks.

710
00:46:23,844 --> 00:46:25,178
My Da-reum.

711
00:46:25,804 --> 00:46:27,389
Look after her for me, Mr. Kang.

712
00:46:27,931 --> 00:46:29,766
She hasn't worked for that long

713
00:46:29,850 --> 00:46:31,810
so she has a lot to learn.

714
00:46:32,310 --> 00:46:33,436
Not a lot, actually.

715
00:46:34,229 --> 00:46:35,272
Just a bit.

716
00:46:36,273 --> 00:46:37,274
She lacks just a bit.

717
00:46:38,650 --> 00:46:40,944
She's diligent
and hard-working, though.

718
00:46:41,278 --> 00:46:42,863
All my employees work hard.

719
00:46:47,617 --> 00:46:49,578
I guess you have nothing good

720
00:46:49,953 --> 00:46:52,122
to say about my Da-reum.

721
00:46:55,917 --> 00:46:57,043
Ms. Da-reum

722
00:46:58,086 --> 00:46:59,462
is an exemplary employee.

723
00:47:01,882 --> 00:47:03,258
She's always so cheerful

724
00:47:03,717 --> 00:47:05,510
and she gives every task her all.

725
00:47:05,594 --> 00:47:09,264
She hasn't been with us very long,
but she's already been a huge help.

726
00:47:10,223 --> 00:47:11,641
You don't have to worry.

727
00:47:13,476 --> 00:47:15,770
My gosh. Is that so?

728
00:47:17,272 --> 00:47:20,609
I thought she was kind
and warmhearted.

729
00:47:21,151 --> 00:47:23,737
She must've gotten that from you.

730
00:47:26,531 --> 00:47:27,532
What?

731
00:47:28,116 --> 00:47:29,492
How did you know that?

732
00:47:30,243 --> 00:47:34,497
People say we're carbon copies
whenever we're out together.

733
00:47:34,581 --> 00:47:36,541
- Do they?
- Oh, let's clink bowls.

734
00:47:36,625 --> 00:47:37,626
Sure.

735
00:47:45,634 --> 00:47:48,803
You're a good drinker, Mr. Kang.

736
00:47:49,804 --> 00:47:51,306
- Have some more.
- Thanks.

737
00:47:55,685 --> 00:47:56,728
Gosh.

738
00:47:57,896 --> 00:47:59,481
- You too.
- Thanks.

739
00:48:01,900 --> 00:48:04,694
So, about my Da-reum.

740
00:48:04,778 --> 00:48:07,280
Is she seeing anyone at work?

741
00:48:08,990 --> 00:48:10,283
Or have a crush on someone?

742
00:48:11,159 --> 00:48:12,244
Pardon?

743
00:48:14,246 --> 00:48:16,414
I don't know anything about that.

744
00:48:17,874 --> 00:48:21,753
I'm worried. She doesn't seem
to care about dating.

745
00:48:25,674 --> 00:48:26,716
By the way

746
00:48:27,175 --> 00:48:29,636
you look incredibly young.

747
00:48:30,262 --> 00:48:33,682
Are you still unmarried?

748
00:48:34,474 --> 00:48:37,227
Unmarried? Yes, I am.

749
00:48:39,145 --> 00:48:40,230
Are you?

750
00:48:42,607 --> 00:48:43,608
Then

751
00:48:43,858 --> 00:48:47,570
what is your ideal kind of woman?

752
00:48:48,280 --> 00:48:49,572
- Pardon?
- You said

753
00:48:49,781 --> 00:48:52,117
Da-reum was kind and warmhearted.

754
00:48:52,909 --> 00:48:55,829
Are you not into that kind of woman?

755
00:48:56,246 --> 00:48:57,872
Well, it's not...

756
00:48:59,457 --> 00:49:00,583
Mom.

757
00:49:01,668 --> 00:49:03,420
Why are you talking nonsense?

758
00:49:03,503 --> 00:49:05,380
Don't grill my boss.

759
00:49:05,463 --> 00:49:09,634
I just wanted to know
what his ideal type was.

760
00:49:09,718 --> 00:49:12,137
You're not supposed to ask that
at work.

761
00:49:12,220 --> 00:49:13,763
There are reasons too.

762
00:49:13,847 --> 00:49:17,434
Did I just get you fired
when you just joined?

763
00:49:17,809 --> 00:49:19,561
- No way.
- What if I did?

764
00:49:19,769 --> 00:49:20,812
<i>Ma'am.</i>

765
00:49:21,604 --> 00:49:23,189
<i>The man your daughter has a crush on.</i>

766
00:49:24,566 --> 00:49:25,608
<i>It's me.</i>

767
00:49:28,862 --> 00:49:30,905
APPELLO

768
00:49:38,455 --> 00:49:39,873
Director.

769
00:49:40,582 --> 00:49:42,292
- Hello.
- Hello.

770
00:49:43,418 --> 00:49:45,253
What brings you here?

771
00:49:45,337 --> 00:49:46,880
I dropped by after a shoot.

772
00:49:47,589 --> 00:49:49,841
Is Marketing busy these days?

773
00:49:50,717 --> 00:49:53,887
The K-Wave project
keeps us here late every day.

774
00:49:57,974 --> 00:49:59,434
Mr. Ha-gi's still here, right?

775
00:49:59,893 --> 00:50:01,269
Mr. Kang's on a business trip.

776
00:50:04,481 --> 00:50:05,482
With Ms. Da-reum.

777
00:50:06,858 --> 00:50:07,859
With Ms. Da-reum?

778
00:50:08,943 --> 00:50:11,613
To sign with a master knot artisan
from Ms. Da-reum's hometown.

779
00:50:12,655 --> 00:50:14,407
They seem to be stuck.

780
00:50:14,491 --> 00:50:16,618
I don't think they'll return
until the deal is signed.

781
00:50:19,037 --> 00:50:20,330
We're ready for the meeting.

782
00:50:20,413 --> 00:50:21,539
- Okay.
- Great.

783
00:50:22,707 --> 00:50:25,085
Director, I have a meeting.

784
00:50:25,168 --> 00:50:26,252
What will you do?

785
00:50:28,838 --> 00:50:31,257
There's no one else here to see.
I'll get going.

786
00:50:31,341 --> 00:50:33,676
- Get back safely, Director.
- Take care.

787
00:50:54,906 --> 00:50:56,741
APPELLO
NAM DA-REUM

788
00:50:56,825 --> 00:50:59,160
MAP TO MOUNT NAMSAN LOCATION,
ROUTE AND EVENT COMMENTS

789
00:51:01,121 --> 00:51:03,623
{\an8}K-WAVE PROJECT
APPELLO WILL WIN! LET'S GO!

790
00:51:19,389 --> 00:51:21,182
<i>A fan of mine drew this character.</i>

791
00:51:21,266 --> 00:51:23,017
It's so cute
that I've got it all memorized.

792
00:51:23,101 --> 00:51:24,769
MONTH-END MARKETING MEETING

793
00:51:45,415 --> 00:51:46,541
It was Da-reum.

794
00:51:50,332 --> 00:51:52,418
Will you really be okay
going home alone?

795
00:51:52,668 --> 00:51:55,045
You're here for work.

796
00:51:55,379 --> 00:51:59,091
Do your best
and win Master Im over, okay?

797
00:51:59,174 --> 00:52:01,844
- Okay. Get home safe, Mom.
- I will.

798
00:52:01,927 --> 00:52:05,681
- Get back safely, ma'am.
- Thank you, Mr. Kang.

799
00:52:05,848 --> 00:52:08,976
- Take care of my daughter for me.
- Don't.

800
00:52:09,143 --> 00:52:10,727
- Bye, Eun-jeong.
- Take care.

801
00:52:10,811 --> 00:52:12,604
- Bye, Mom.
- Bye.

802
00:52:13,480 --> 00:52:15,357
Get home safe.

803
00:52:24,700 --> 00:52:27,828
I'm pleased that you want to learn
how to make these.

804
00:52:28,579 --> 00:52:30,914
I've been doing it for over ten years
but I still find it tough.

805
00:52:31,290 --> 00:52:33,292
Master Im always says

806
00:52:33,500 --> 00:52:35,586
making knots is like
asceticism or meditation.

807
00:52:36,462 --> 00:52:38,964
She did it all her life
and she says it's still hard.

808
00:52:39,548 --> 00:52:42,134
Compared to her,
I barely learned how to walk.

809
00:52:43,260 --> 00:52:44,803
Maybe I'm yet to be born.

810
00:52:45,387 --> 00:52:47,890
Anyway, as you can see here

811
00:52:47,973 --> 00:52:51,560
this is a braided cord,
and it's covered in braided threads.

812
00:52:51,643 --> 00:52:54,396
I'll teach you
how to make a knot out of this.

813
00:52:55,230 --> 00:52:57,566
You must want to get a feel.

814
00:52:57,649 --> 00:52:59,902
Shall we sit over there?

815
00:53:02,029 --> 00:53:04,531
I'll teach you the easiest one.

816
00:53:05,199 --> 00:53:08,911
It's one of the basic knots
called <i>dongsimgyeol</i>.

817
00:53:08,994 --> 00:53:10,412
<i>- Dongsimgyeol.
- Dongsimgyeol.</i>

818
00:53:10,496 --> 00:53:12,664
First, make a knot loop.

819
00:53:12,748 --> 00:53:16,168
Knot loops are these large holes.

820
00:53:16,251 --> 00:53:18,670
Take the two strands that are hanging

821
00:53:18,962 --> 00:53:22,007
and put them between
the second and third loops.

822
00:53:22,090 --> 00:53:24,343
- Like this?
- That's perfect.

823
00:53:24,426 --> 00:53:26,011
You're doing well.

824
00:53:30,349 --> 00:53:31,850
And then...

825
00:53:33,101 --> 00:53:34,353
This one...

826
00:53:35,395 --> 00:53:38,565
This goes up and fold...

827
00:53:38,649 --> 00:53:41,443
Do I fold this one or that one?

828
00:53:42,361 --> 00:53:44,154
This... Hang on.

829
00:53:44,530 --> 00:53:46,615
You did it wrong.

830
00:53:50,744 --> 00:53:52,246
It's not like this.

831
00:53:52,329 --> 00:53:54,665
- This goes in here.
- Oh, that one?

832
00:53:54,748 --> 00:53:56,833
- That goes first?
- And then

833
00:53:57,501 --> 00:53:59,169
you slip this in here.

834
00:53:59,253 --> 00:54:00,754
- Oh, this...
- In here.

835
00:54:00,837 --> 00:54:03,340
- In the middle.
- Wait. Like this?

836
00:54:04,216 --> 00:54:06,635
It's done. Oh, like this?

837
00:54:49,469 --> 00:54:50,679
TRAINING COMPLETION CEREMONY

838
00:54:56,810 --> 00:54:59,646
We did it. It's done.

839
00:55:01,857 --> 00:55:03,775
After making this myself

840
00:55:04,484 --> 00:55:07,070
it looks extra pretty
and I'm so proud of it.

841
00:55:08,905 --> 00:55:09,948
It does.

842
00:55:11,533 --> 00:55:13,327
I get what she meant

843
00:55:13,744 --> 00:55:15,537
when she said it merges with time.

844
00:55:18,040 --> 00:55:21,209
I didn't know so much work
went into making such a small knot.

845
00:55:39,978 --> 00:55:41,521
I tried to manage on my own.

846
00:55:41,855 --> 00:55:43,231
Thank you.

847
00:55:44,066 --> 00:55:45,192
It's fine.

848
00:55:45,275 --> 00:55:47,235
Tell us if you need help
with anything.

849
00:55:48,528 --> 00:55:51,490
All my fellow students have left.

850
00:55:51,948 --> 00:55:54,868
I'm the last remaining successor.

851
00:55:56,119 --> 00:55:57,412
If I were to quit too

852
00:55:58,288 --> 00:55:59,665
this skill will die out.

853
00:56:06,880 --> 00:56:10,384
Please persuade Master Im for me.

854
00:56:13,720 --> 00:56:17,933
It's a matter of time
before we lose all the artisans.

855
00:56:18,892 --> 00:56:21,853
The work is intense,
and we barely make a living.

856
00:56:22,896 --> 00:56:23,939
Who would do this?

857
00:56:25,482 --> 00:56:27,359
Factory-made or handmade

858
00:56:27,442 --> 00:56:30,320
I just want people to know
about traditional knots.

859
00:56:36,576 --> 00:56:38,912
Is this what you thought all along?

860
00:56:39,663 --> 00:56:40,747
Master Im.

861
00:56:41,915 --> 00:56:43,417
If that's how you think, leave.

862
00:56:44,501 --> 00:56:47,379
Make knots at a factory
and make a fortune!

863
00:56:49,089 --> 00:56:50,257
"Make a fortune"?

864
00:56:51,967 --> 00:56:55,429
I'd have quit long ago
if that's what I wanted.

865
00:56:56,471 --> 00:56:59,683
I do this
to keep the tradition alive.

866
00:57:00,475 --> 00:57:02,269
We need all the help we can get.

867
00:57:02,728 --> 00:57:03,895
I at least...

868
00:57:06,314 --> 00:57:07,524
Why do you say

869
00:57:08,024 --> 00:57:09,860
I'm wrong just because

870
00:57:10,444 --> 00:57:12,446
I take a different approach
to protect it?

871
00:57:46,313 --> 00:57:47,355
Ms. Da-reum.

872
00:57:48,231 --> 00:57:49,858
Yes?

873
00:57:50,484 --> 00:57:53,069
Can you come outside?

874
00:57:55,197 --> 00:57:56,281
Give me a moment.

875
00:58:05,624 --> 00:58:08,627
I stuck them in the fire earlier
and didn't want to eat them alone.

876
00:58:09,127 --> 00:58:11,379
Roasted sweet potatoes.

877
00:58:12,047 --> 00:58:13,715
I didn't know you like this.

878
00:58:21,056 --> 00:58:22,641
Have a taste.

879
00:58:24,851 --> 00:58:27,187
- It smells amazing.
- Watch out. It's hot.

880
00:58:31,733 --> 00:58:33,193
Ms. Da-reum, are you all right?

881
00:58:35,070 --> 00:58:36,154
Spit it out here.

882
00:58:39,407 --> 00:58:42,118
<i>Why is he holding out his hands?</i>

883
00:58:43,245 --> 00:58:44,955
No, it's fine.

884
00:58:58,218 --> 00:58:59,636
Take your time. Don't hurt yourself.

885
00:59:00,929 --> 00:59:02,013
Thank you.

886
00:59:12,983 --> 00:59:16,778
<i>Why is Mr. Kang so nice to me?</i>

887
00:59:24,744 --> 00:59:26,162
It reminds me of my grandma.

888
00:59:27,664 --> 00:59:30,917
She used to roast me
sweet potatoes like this.

889
00:59:35,171 --> 00:59:36,339
It must be nice...

890
00:59:38,133 --> 00:59:40,051
to have a kind grandma

891
00:59:41,094 --> 00:59:42,387
and a mother.

892
00:59:45,515 --> 00:59:46,600
Thanks to you

893
00:59:47,517 --> 00:59:48,852
I enjoyed today.

894
00:59:50,312 --> 00:59:51,354
What did you enjoy?

895
00:59:55,483 --> 00:59:57,277
Drinking with your mother.

896
01:00:03,116 --> 01:00:04,910
My mom died when I was
a high-school senior.

897
01:00:07,245 --> 01:00:08,622
I never got to do that.

898
01:00:21,968 --> 01:00:25,013
You can scratch that
off your bucket list.

899
01:00:27,057 --> 01:00:28,141
I can.

900
01:00:31,436 --> 01:00:32,479
What about you?

901
01:00:33,229 --> 01:00:34,272
Do you have a bucket list?

902
01:00:39,945 --> 01:00:41,988
Sit in the front row at a concert?

903
01:00:43,531 --> 01:00:45,033
Have a pet?

904
01:00:45,408 --> 01:00:46,409
And to hear

905
01:00:47,410 --> 01:00:48,662
someone say to me

906
01:00:49,579 --> 01:00:54,125
that they're glad to have me around.

907
01:01:00,799 --> 01:01:02,384
It's corny, isn't it?

908
01:01:30,412 --> 01:01:31,663
I must've been by the fire
for too long.

909
01:01:33,665 --> 01:01:34,708
It's hot.

910
01:01:35,792 --> 01:01:37,669
- I'll take a stroll.
- Okay.

911
01:01:45,635 --> 01:01:46,636
What about you?

912
01:01:49,139 --> 01:01:50,140
Would you like

913
01:01:51,141 --> 01:01:52,142
to come with me on a walk?

914
01:02:01,609 --> 01:02:02,736
I have a feeling

915
01:02:04,654 --> 01:02:06,239
I'll remember today for a long time.

916
01:02:08,074 --> 01:02:09,075
Me too.

917
01:02:10,744 --> 01:02:12,203
I'm glad that you were here...

918
01:02:14,497 --> 01:02:15,623
with me.

919
01:02:20,920 --> 01:02:23,548
You took something off
my bucket list.

920
01:02:33,099 --> 01:02:34,225
Ms. Da-reum.

921
01:02:36,644 --> 01:02:38,188
You told me before

922
01:02:39,105 --> 01:02:40,440
that you joined Appello

923
01:02:42,150 --> 01:02:44,110
because there was someone
you wanted to meet.

924
01:02:47,655 --> 01:02:48,740
Yes, well...

925
01:02:49,157 --> 01:02:50,366
That was true then.

926
01:02:51,326 --> 01:02:54,162
<i>What's going on?
Why is he asking me that?</i>

927
01:02:54,621 --> 01:02:55,789
Be honest with me today.

928
01:02:58,666 --> 01:02:59,959
The person you wanted to meet.

929
01:03:01,002 --> 01:03:02,170
Was it me?

930
01:03:05,548 --> 01:03:06,549
Pardon?

931
01:03:09,344 --> 01:03:10,678
Do you see me as a man?

932
01:03:11,846 --> 01:03:14,808
Do you think

933
01:03:15,391 --> 01:03:19,521
that I'm interested in you?

934
01:03:21,940 --> 01:03:24,442
It's just us two here. We can be...

935
01:03:24,526 --> 01:03:25,527
No, wait.

936
01:03:26,152 --> 01:03:27,237
Just a moment.

937
01:03:27,737 --> 01:03:29,030
Is that why you said

938
01:03:29,364 --> 01:03:32,158
you were the CEO
and I was an employee

939
01:03:32,242 --> 01:03:33,785
and tried to keep your distance?

940
01:03:37,914 --> 01:03:40,250
Was that really the reason?

941
01:03:44,963 --> 01:03:49,884
I know very well
that we can never be.

942
01:03:50,718 --> 01:03:53,263
I know so well who you like.

943
01:03:56,015 --> 01:03:57,016
I did what?

944
01:04:00,603 --> 01:04:01,604
Who could that be?

945
01:04:04,274 --> 01:04:06,609
Oh, well...

946
01:04:11,948 --> 01:04:13,533
Who do I like?

947
01:04:22,500 --> 01:04:24,711
You have a thing
for Director Lee Chan.

948
01:04:25,128 --> 01:04:28,381
- What?
- For a long time.

949
01:04:31,259 --> 01:04:32,343
What the...

950
01:04:32,969 --> 01:04:34,304
Excuse me?

951
01:04:34,387 --> 01:04:36,055
Don't you worry.

952
01:04:36,222 --> 01:04:39,350
I'll guard your feelings for you.

953
01:04:39,642 --> 01:04:42,061
I'm not prejudiced at all.

954
01:04:46,608 --> 01:04:47,859
Wait, Ms. Da-reum.

955
01:04:48,776 --> 01:04:49,986
All this while

956
01:04:50,570 --> 01:04:54,073
you thought I liked men?

957
01:04:57,577 --> 01:04:58,661
But you do.

958
01:05:04,667 --> 01:05:05,919
Ms. Da-reum.

959
01:05:06,419 --> 01:05:08,129
I'm not into men.

960
01:05:09,172 --> 01:05:10,548
- What?
- Also...

961
01:05:12,425 --> 01:05:14,302
there's this woman
I'm interested in right now.

962
01:05:17,263 --> 01:05:18,264
What?

963
01:06:27,834 --> 01:06:31,754
{\an8}MY BIAS, MY BOSS

964
01:06:42,557 --> 01:06:45,351
{\an8}EPILOGUE

965
01:06:49,939 --> 01:06:51,065
Shall we pull?

966
01:06:52,984 --> 01:06:55,028
Oh, yes.

967
01:06:58,656 --> 01:06:59,782
It's done.

968
01:07:05,079 --> 01:07:06,497
Do you know how to do it now?

969
01:07:07,874 --> 01:07:10,001
Try it yourself.

970
01:07:17,508 --> 01:07:20,011
It's the first thing
we made together.

971
01:07:21,179 --> 01:07:23,014
Was it called <i>dongsimgyeol</i>?

972
01:07:31,397 --> 01:07:32,398
Why are you so surprised?

973
01:07:34,859 --> 01:07:35,860
I'm not.

974
01:07:50,375 --> 01:07:53,127
<i>DONGSIMGYEOL </i>KNOT

975
01:07:53,211 --> 01:07:55,129
TO BE OF ONE HEART FOREVER

976
01:07:55,213 --> 01:07:56,964
WISHES FOR ETERNAL LOVE AND PEACE

977
01:07:57,423 --> 01:07:59,217
{\an8}<i>Who is the woman he's interested in?</i>

978
01:08:00,426 --> 01:08:02,762
{\an8}- Let's go in my car.
- Come with me.

979
01:08:04,097 --> 01:08:05,598
{\an8}<i>What's this plot twist?</i>

980
01:08:05,681 --> 01:08:07,433
{\an8}<i>"You're the woman I'm interested in."</i>

981
01:08:07,517 --> 01:08:09,769
{\an8}Why can't you say it? Why?

982
01:08:10,144 --> 01:08:13,856
{\an8}How about we stay
by each other's side from now on?

983
01:08:16,359 --> 01:08:17,610
{\an8}<i>Who did she go to see?</i>

984
01:08:18,236 --> 01:08:19,445
{\an8}You're so handsome.

985
01:08:19,529 --> 01:08:22,073
{\an8}<i>- Don't be with a guy like that.
- Mr. Kang.</i>

986
01:08:22,615 --> 01:08:25,159
{\an8}It's okay to tell me
that you're not okay.

987
01:08:28,450 --> 01:08:30,452
{\an8}Subtitles by Eunjin Erica Kim
and Jennifer Jean Lim

988
01:08:30,533 --> 01:08:32,735
{\an8}Synced and corrected by
WEISSACHsubs

